# Repo-owned plugin boundary

- Treat this repository's plugin surface as a checked-in manifest plus explicit
	references to `rules`, `skills`, `.cursor/agents`, `.cursor/hooks.json`, and
	`.cursor/state`.
- Treat `skills/phase-controller/SKILL.md` and `.cursor/agents/orchestrator.md`
	as the orchestration entry points. Other skills and agents are workers in
	that lifecycle.
- Keep shipped hooks bounded to short lifecycle helpers. `claim-guard.py` and
	`stop-gate.py` may read local workflow state; they must not become hidden
	daemons.
- Keep shipped agents bounded to checked-in prompts and validators. Do not
	imply background-worker provisioning unless matching Cursor product support,
	artifacts, and validators land together.
- Keep local plugin instructions aligned with `docs/local-plugin-verification.md`
	and `~/.cursor/plugins/local` as a manual user-environment verification path.
- When plugin ownership claims change, update validator scripts and
	`docs/references.md` in the same edit.
